 "summary": [
  {
   "_key": "en",
   "value": "The History Of Taba Taba, nestled in the Sinai Peninsula, has been a pivotal junction since ancient times. Like many areas in Sinai, it served as a crucial meeting point for trading caravans that traversed the deserts, connecting the Arabia"
  },
  {
